## Adding a skill

Use the bundled `create-skill` skill. Individual skill authoring does not
belong to the repository lifecycle tool.

## Versioning

`skills-repo.config.json`'s `package.version` owns the aggregate release.
Each skill owns its release in `SKILL.md` under `metadata.version` (a quoted
SemVer string). All plugin manifests and marketplace listings mirror these
sources. Private npm tooling versions and schema/template versions are separate.

```sh
node scripts/version-skills.mjs check
node scripts/version-skills.mjs bump example-skill patch --dry-run
node scripts/version-skills.mjs bump example-skill patch
node scripts/version-skills.mjs bump package minor
node scripts/version-skills.mjs sync
```

Use patch for fixes, minor for compatible additions, and major for breaking
changes. A skill bump also patches the aggregate plugin so whole-package
installations see the release. Bump once per release; use `package major` too
when the aggregate has breaking changes. `sync` repairs mirrors without a bump,
and migrates missing skill metadata from existing marketplace versions.
`check` compares release versions only, remains read-only, and lets unrelated
dependency updates proceed; CI rejects version drift. No command commits, tags, pushes,
or publishes.
After adding or removing a skill, bump the aggregate package before publishing.

Use this helper instead of editing managed manifests or configuration by hand:
it preserves managed hashes and rejects conflicting edits. After a release,
the repository generator's `sync` preserves published skill versions.
Skill metadata does not pin an installer; use an immutable Git ref when needed.

